  "report_period": "Week 11 (8th Mar to 15th Mar 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Nicholas G Moundreas Shipping have committed their Capesize \"Epic\" 180/2010 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 32,5 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Sealink\" 180/2010 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 31 mill. Furthermore, following the sale of the \"Castillo De Valverde\" 173/2005 Bohai, China (SS 12/2025, DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) at USD 15,8 mill, Mssrs Empresa Naviera Elcano committed the sister vessel \"Castillo De Catoira\" 173/2005 Bohai, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at high USD 16 mill. In addition, GENCO sold their \"Genco Maximus\" 169/2009 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) & \"Genco Claudius\" 169/2010 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to clients of Golden Union at USD 47 mill enbloc, while the sister vessel \"Enco Ommodus\" 169/2009 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold earlier this month at USD 22,5 mill. The Panamax \"Ying Hao 02\" 75/2012 Guangzhou, China (SS 06/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) of Dongguan Yinghao Shipping was committed at USD 16,8 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Zhong Xin Pearl\" 75/2013 Guangzhou, China (SS 09/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at the same price. On the Supramax sector, Anthony Giavridis Maritime committed their \"Gant Muse\" 56/2004 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) to Vietnamese interests at low-mid USD 11 mill. Note that a month ago, the sister vessel \"SSI Challenger\" 56/2004 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 10,7 mill. Briese Shipping committed their Handysize \"BBC Pluto\" 37/2010 Tianjin, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) to Turkish interests at USD 11,7 mill. For reference, the \"Clipper Copenhagen\" 37/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 06/2025, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) was sold back in December at USD 11,2 mill.",
    "tankers": "SK Shipping have committed their VLCC \"C. Vision\" 314/2004 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 06/2024, Scrubber fitted) for USD 33,5 mill, while the Japanese built \"Achelous\" 299/2004 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, Scrubber fitted) of Teodor Oceanic was committed at USD 30 mill. The MR2 \"Glenda Melanie\" 47/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) of d'Amico Tankers was committed to Chinese interests at USD 27,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Ocios Ioannis\" 47/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in November at USD 25 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 12,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 17,000/20,000 pd range. A number of Indonesia and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 16,000/19.000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/21,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/800K pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 23,000/25,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips via South America were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 19,000/21,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 900K/1M. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 18,800 pd 6/8 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesia trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Continental trips via West Africa into India were fixed around usd 20,000/21,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean with scrap were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/800K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Continental trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Trips from Baltic into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. Trips from Black Sea into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 10,000/13,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Caribbean were reported at the level of usd 9,000/10,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
